.TH TAEMA-LEARNING 7 "2026-10-21" "taema 0.4.0" "Tæma Manual"
.SH NAME
taema-learning \- learning, provenance, review, and recovery
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tæma records validated application identities, owner-to-survivor pairs, stable survivor
signatures, reviews, vetoes, and retained action outcomes in a per-user SQLite database.
The daemon remains the single writer; CLI views open the database read-only while it runs.
The audit log records decisions and their authorization reasons.
.PP
A pair connects one application identity (the owner) with one survivor key. A signature
describes a survivor set by its sorted member keys and counts, runtime-directory hash,
terminal state, and owner. Process IDs and start times do not affect a signature. An explicit
signature answer applies to an identical relaunched survivor set; a changed set is reviewed
and cannot inherit authority for a new member.
.SH INSPECTING LEARNING
.TP
.B taema learn show
Show a summary of apps, pairs, and signatures.
.TP
.B taema learn apps
List validated application identities and retained evidence.
.TP
.B taema learn pairs
List owner-to-survivor decisions, confidence, counts, and reasons.
.TP
.B taema learn signatures
List survivor signatures, explicit answers, and stop outcomes.
.TP
.B taema learn show --legacy
List quarantined legacy answers that need confirmation.
.TP
.B taema why TARGET
Explain provenance, evidence, matching signatures, vetoes, and possible actions.
.SH ANSWERING AND OVERRULING
.TP
.B taema review
List pending close and provenance reviews.
.TP
.B taema answer ID CHOICE
Answer a review with \fBstop\fR, \fBkeep\fR, \fBstandalone\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B taema teach OWNER SURVIVOR CHOICE
Record an explicit pair answer without waiting for a review.
.TP
.B taema do-not-kill TARGET
Create a durable veto. Pending vetoes are enforced while the daemon is down.
.TP
.B taema undo [ID]
Reverse a retained automatic action. Undoing a stop adds keep evidence and a veto, clears
pending stop state, and suspends matching automatic authority during the regret interval.
.TP
.B taema forget --all APP
Remove an app's learned records while retaining its vetoes.
.SH AUTOMATIC OUTCOMES
The learner records successful stops, respawns, and regret against the matching pair and
signature. Regret means the same pair or signature returned during its configured window;
it adds keep evidence and suspends automatic authority. Outcomes do not override hard
protection, dependencies, holds, or vetoes. Self-derived stop authority is disabled by
default.
.SH STORAGE AND MIGRATION
The default state directory is
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/taema
or
.IR ~/.local/state/taema .
It contains \fBstate.db\fR, the append-only \fBdecisions.log\fR, and pending offline
feedback. Database files are private to the user. On the first 0.4.0 start, valid 0.3.0
JSON learning is imported transactionally; invalid-owner answers become reviews. The
importer keeps the source and creates a mode-0600 \fBknowledge.json.backup-*\fR file before
committing. Migration does not stop processes. See
.I /usr/share/doc/taema/legacy-state-migration.md
and
.I /usr/share/doc/taema/state-schema.md
for upgrade and schema details.
.PP
To prepare a downgrade to 0.2, export the compatible JSON format before stopping the
daemon:
.PP
.RS
.B taema learn export --format v2 --output "$HOME/taema-knowledge-v2.json"
.RE
.PP
Keep the SQLite database and its sidecars as a rollback copy. The migration guide describes
how to restore the exported file for a 0.2 downgrade.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/taema/state.db
SQLite learning, provenance, review, veto, and decision state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/taema/decisions.log
Human-readable JSON Lines audit events.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/taema/knowledge.json.backup-*
Private source backup retained for 30 days after legacy import.
